ine_run_until_blocked_budget_10_small_workflow/allocations.tsv\nHOST/VARIANCE/ADVERSE OBSERVATIONS:\n# Independent R131 performance DATA review\n\nVerdict: ACCEPT limited to recorded-session MEAN comparisons for the three declared IR-interpreter metrics. No data/arithmetic/provenance finding in this bounded review. This does not establish causal speedup, individual-operation tail latency, a noise-free host, generated/maxperf, release readiness, or whole-product acceptance. Publisher CODE review is separate.\n\nOnly actual R131 session02 is accepted: `/home/lewis/tmp/vb-f1f5-final-benchmark-r131/session02`. Candidate pin is `072e8ddd2733f971c55393ad9a477d9dac91e0a4`, baseline is `7f505d498fa35acb5b70b083ac6f02cd40f3a891` plus the approved frozen fixture/harness overlay. This uses the actual new R131 samples and fresh build/preflight receipts, not retagged R121 data. Both actual Cargo benchmark receipts identify the correct source roots and `fresh: false`; builds and real-operation preflights exit 0. Identical binary hashes across different sessions are retained as observed; no old session samples are substituted.\n\nProtocol R2 SHA256 `e010e657398fc253d3106d319853e7da5c7c770d0746b373dab1c27af9dc1ffe` is unchanged. Complete ABBA order A1/B1/B2/A2, CPU14, 100 samples per metric per run, 3-second warmup, 5-second measurement. All four latency phases and candidate-only counter phase exit 0. All 12 actual latency logs contain only the intended benchmark, the required sample count/warmup, and no observed execution error. Twelve raw new/sample.json arrays plus their associated estimates/metadata were checked; base/ copies match their corresponding new/ copies. All 1,200 measured samples remain included, including reported outliers.\n\n| Metric | Baseline mean ps | Candidate mean ps | Mean delta | Unchanged allowed regression |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| SaveConst step | 45247 | 38233 | -15.501176360% | 3% |\n| IPC frame decode | 73559 | 71503 | -2.795320494% | 5% |\n| Budgeted engine run | 67699 | 57798 | -14.625773929% | 3% |\n\nIndependent exact-rational recalculation parses the original decimal JSON tokens, takes the arithmetic mean of the two original unrounded Criterion mean.point_estimate values per side with equal run weighting, and converts/rounds that final side mean once to integer picoseconds. Each per-run estimate also agrees with its raw sample-mean arithmetic within floating-point serialization tolerance. Recalculated means match the supplied aggregate. The configured 3/5/3 ceilings match the current perf-budget policy; no thresholds changed. All four possible A/B per-run mean pairings also remain within those limits, recorded as observations, not an extra acceptance requirement or selected subset.\n\nP50/P95/P99 are nearest-rank quantiles of all 200 pooled time/iterations sample means per side, ranks 100/190/198, not individual-operation tails. All supplied quantiles match independent raw recomputation. For this session every pooled quantile decreases, and all four per-run p99 cross-pair comparisons decrease. Thus no adverse pooled/per-run p99 was omitted here; no adverse observation from a different session is silently substituted or claimed to describe R131. Run variance is visible, especially the baseline IPC A1 upper sample means and differing baseline engine distributions. Quantile and mean observations do not justify a causal explanation.\n\nEvery actual source-before/source-after/invocation agrees with the relevant build source and pin. Independent git ls-tree/cat-file scans checked all actual tracked relevant file bytes and modes against the pins: 2,178 baseline inputs and 2,573 candidate inputs. The only allowed baseline difference is the exact approved benchmark postimage; candidate relevant tracked bytes match its pin. Recomputed performance fingerprints: baseline `af0335bf81f5c6c07679fc6a1c34aaaeb6bedc36ca8a36b790223aaa2ca41a7f`, candidate `3f59b48e83f6d69b9e24297754533912967f7f439d0dd2168e2888ac4ad686af`